# `if (knot.part)`: a read that tests its receiver for itself, at the end of its block, outside of loops, and nothing but the truth of what it reads is asked.
# The slot is held to a type, and whoever stores goes by it: so on the way on which the receiver passes, the word in the slot and that type say the answer, and the way leads to the targets of the branch at once.
# Nothing is boxed there, no type is tested and no stub is asked: the read has no value in which ways could meet. Only what is read by name is a value, and it goes by the tests that stand behind the read.
# `open` lies in the Extension, which is read in line: where the Extension has no room for the slot the way leads on as from an empty slot, so there too no two ways meet in a value.
# The cast lays Leaf above what the constructor function makes: by it the slots of the fields that are stored behind the making are held to what Leaf writes.
# What such readers answer under every lie from out of sight: answers/slot-answers-for-the-truth-of-what-it-holds.ts.
# f6 = asksPart, f7 = asksOpen
# -- source: knots.ts
